= Los representantes de casilla

The registro bought you a line on the ballot; it did not buy you honest arithmetic. That is built by hand, precinct by precinct, in the least glamorous work the Party does: finding the schoolteacher, the housewife, the retired railwayman who will sit at a casilla from dawn until the count is signed — refuse the torta and the twenty pesos, and put their name to a tally the machine cannot quietly improve. A representante on every table is worth more than a manifesto. It is the difference between a fraud that happens and a fraud that gets *caught.*

The list of the willing grows one conversation at a time, and it grows fastest where the Movement is already rooted: where the colonias are organized and the campesinos are with you, the recruiters find takers; where the Party is thin, the tables stay uncovered and the urns travel unwatched.

- @reclutar_casilla: Recruit and train them, colonia by colonia — the slow skeleton the whole electoral road stands on.
- @root: Not this month.
- @easy_discard

